      "writtenOn": "2022-10-05T01:56:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay so that makes sense and it works, but I think it\u0027s a bit unobvious locally. You could add a comment saying\n\n  // Callback will be unregistered in tearDown()\n\nThat being said if you ask me I don\u0027t think that such a comment is more useful than a call to unregisterCallback() ; in fact I think the call is more obvious. Plus, you don\u0027t know how often this will be called and if it\u0027s called a lot all of these callbacks count toward the 100 callbacks limit per process, so you might run into problems here eventually. All in all, I would still unregister here.\n\nBut up to you, I\u0027m happy with either your current code, or a comment, or the call to unregister.",
      "parentUuid": "c9f9f5de_6c73e00e",
